Package: goodix-533c-test
Version: 0.0.1~test1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-usb, python3-pycryptodome, openssl, udev
Maintainer: daemonhorn <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/daemonhorn/goodix-533c-re
Description: TEST/EXPERIMENTAL capture tool for Goodix 27c6:533c fingerprint sensor
 Standalone diagnostic tool that reproduces the closed-source vendor
 driver's USB wire protocol for the Goodix 27c6:533c ("53xc" family)
 fingerprint sensor, using an open-source reimplementation, and captures
 a raw image from the sensor for inspection.
 .
 THIS IS NOT A LIBFPRINT DRIVER. It does NOT integrate with fprintd,
 PAM, GNOME/KDE login, screen unlock, or sudo authentication. It only
 proves the protocol works and produces a .pgm image file via the
 `goodix-533c-capture` command line tool.
 .
 Image quality (visible fingerprint ridge detail) is confirmed on the
 original driver author's hardware but was NOT fully reproduced on a
 second independent unit at time of packaging -- see the project
 homepage for current status before relying on this for anything.
 .
 Driver code is from an unmerged upstream pull request (nikicat,
 goodix-fp-linux-dev/goodix-fp-dump#75); this package exists to make
 that work easy to test, not as an endorsement that it is finished.
